      "message": "\u003e I can already push a commit from jj to gerrit without a change-id footer.\n\nNot unless you have `receive.requireChangeId` set to `false`? Or requiring the `jj gerrit upload` command to add a change-id for you, is that what you meant? But then there are no issues with follow-up patch-sets as far as I\u0027m aware.\n\nThis change would allow you to push changes from JJ without requiring a `Change-Id` in the commit footer at all. Gerrit would recognise the `change-id` header and use that as the identifier.",
