      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tested it now: just created a new Gerrit site with all default init options. The requireChangeId was set to true in All-Projects. I was able to push a new change from jj using `jj gerrit upload`. Locally the commit didn\u0027t have Change-Id. In Gerrit I see that the Change-Id footer was added. This is the same behaviour I observed when uploading to gerrit-review using jj.\n\nNow I remember the main issue: If I download such a patch-set then I have that change duplicated in jj, one with and one without Change-Id... and then I have to abandon one. This is why, for now, I configured my local jj to always add Change-Id to the commit message. Would that scenario be fixed?",
