      "message": "\u003e The user makes changes and runs jj gerrit upload again. This time the change ID is xyz. It creates a new change instead of uploading a new patchset to the old change because the old change used abc.\n\nJust to confirm I understand correctly, this would only be the case if the user actively removed the `Change-Id` footer from the commit message. If he just edits the commit and leaves that footer in the place, then the footer would take precedence.",
