      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T10:38:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Just to confirm I understand correctly, this would only be the case if the user actively removed the Change-Id footer from the commit message. If he just edits the commit and leaves that footer in the place, then the footer would take precedence.\n\nYou are understanding correctly, but there\u0027s a part that you\u0027ve missed. Change-ID footers in JJ are ephemeral. When I run `jj gerrit upload`, it:\n* Starts a transaction\n* Adds the footer to the description\n* Uploads that amended commit\n* Abandons the transaction\n\nSo changing the jj code to not add the footer would actually be equivalent to deleting the footer from existing commits when you re-upload them.",
      "parentUuid": "2fb3adf0_0b7e5fa1",
      "revId": "17c127e740db54df6973d19b2757dac95c3a46fa",
